\appendix

\section{Proof of the Poincar\'e inequality}\label{app:poincare}

For $\Omega \subset (0, \ell) \times \R^{d-1}$ and $v \in C_c^\infty(\Omega)$,
the fundamental theorem of calculus and the Cauchy--Schwarz inequality give
\[
  \abs{v(x)}^2 = \abs{\int_0^{x_1} \partial_1 v(s, x') \, \dd s}^2
  \le \ell \int_0^\ell \abs{\partial_1 v(s, x')}^2 \, \dd s ,
\]
and integrating over $\Omega$ proves \cref{lem:poincare} with $C_P = \ell$.
Density extends it to all of $H_0^1(\Omega)$.

