the spacing commands, the text blocks, lists four deep, notes, counters,
lengths, a document's own commands and blocks, boxes, tables, LaTeX's own
picture, and mathematics of every kind.

\subsection{Headings}\label{app:headings}

\subsubsection{A subsubsection}
Text under a subsubsection.

\paragraph{A paragraph heading.} Run in, as LaTeX's are.

\subparagraph{A subparagraph.} Run in and indented.

\subsubsection*{An unnumbered subsubsection}
Text under it.

\subsection{Faces and sizes}

Families: {\rmfamily roman}, {\sffamily sans serif}, {\ttfamily typewriter};
series: {\bfseries bold}, {\mdseries medium}; shapes: {\itshape italic},
{\slshape slanted}, {\scshape small capitals}, {\upshape upright}, and
{\normalfont the normal face}. The same as commands: \textrm{roman},
\textsf{sans}, \texttt{mono}, \textbf{bold}, \textmd{medium}, \textit{italic},
\textsl{slanted}, \textsc{caps}, \textup{upright}, \textnormal{normal},
\emph{emphasised} and {\em emphasised too}, and \underline{underlined}.
Combined: \textbf{\textit{bold italic}} and \textsf{\textbf{bold sans}}.
Sizes, every one: {\tiny tiny} {\scriptsize scriptsize} {\footnotesize
footnotesize} {\small small} {\normalsize normalsize} {\large large}
{\Large Large} {\LARGE LARGE} {\huge huge} {\Huge Huge}.

\subsection{Characters}

Accents on every vowel they take: \'a \'e \'{\i} \'o \'u, \`a \`e \`o,
\^a \^e \^o, \"a \"e \"o \"u, \~a \~n \~o, \=a \=o, \.z, \u{a}, \v{c} \v{s}
\v{z}, \H{o}, \c{c} \c{s}, \d{a}, \b{a}, \r{a} and \t{oo}. Letters of other
alphabets: \ae{} \AE{} \oe{} \OE{} \aa{} \AA{} \o{} \O{} \l{} \L{} \ss{}
\i{} \j. Specials written as text: \# \$ \% \& \_ \{ \} \textbackslash{}
\textasciitilde{} \textasciicircum{} \textbar{} \textless{} \textgreater{}.
Punctuation: ``double quotes'', `single quotes', a hyphen-ated word, an en
dash 1--2, an em dash---so, an ellipsis\ldots{} and \dots, \S\,1, \P,
\dag, \ddag, \textbullet, \textperiodcentered, \copyright, \textregistered,
\texttrademark, \pounds, \guillemotleft{}guillemets\guillemotright, and
\slash{} between words. The logos \TeX, \LaTeX{} and \LaTeXe, and today,
\today.

\subsection{Spacing}

Horizontal space: a\,b (thin), a\:b (medium), a\;b (thick), a\ b
(control space), a\quad b, a\qquad b, a\enspace b, a\hspace{1cm}b and a
negative one, a\hspace{-0.5em}b; a~tie keeps words together. Lines filled:
\noindent Left\hfill Right\par
\noindent Dots\dotfill there\par
\noindent Rule\hrulefill here\par
Vertical space: a small skip,\smallskip\par a medium one,\medskip\par a big
one,\bigskip\par and a set one.\vspace{6pt}\par Line breaks without a new
paragraph:\\ a second line\newline and a third; \linebreak a break asked
for, and a word that may break where marked: in\-con\-ceiv\-able.
Invisible material keeps its room: [\phantom{hidden}], [\hphantom{wide}],
[\vphantom{Tall}x] and \smash{smashed}.

\subsection{Text blocks}

\begin{center}
Centred text, a line at a time.\\ A second centred line.
\end{center}
\begin{flushleft}
Flush left, ragged right.
\end{flushleft}
\begin{flushright}
Flush right, ragged left.
\end{flushright}
\begin{quote}
A short quotation, indented on both sides.
\end{quote}
\begin{quotation}
A longer quotation, its paragraphs indented as well as its margins.

Its second paragraph.
\end{quotation}
\begin{verse}
A verse, its lines as written,\\
and turned over when too long\\
for the measure it is set in.
\end{verse}
{\centering A centred paragraph by declaration.\par}
{\raggedright A paragraph ragged right by declaration, long enough to
show its right edge left uneven.\par}
{\raggedleft A paragraph ragged left.\par}

\begin{tabbing}
Name \= Role \= Since \kill
Ada \> engines \> 1843 \\
Alan \> machines \> 1936
\end{tabbing}

\subsection{Lists, four deep}

\begin{enumerate}
\item First level, numbered.
  \begin{enumerate}
  \item Second level, lettered.
    \begin{enumerate}
    \item Third level, in Roman numerals.
      \begin{enumerate}
      \item Fourth level, in capitals.
      \end{enumerate}
    \end{enumerate}
  \end{enumerate}
\item[$\star$] An item with a label of its own.
\item\label{item:last} An item referred to later.
\end{enumerate}
\begin{itemize}
\item A bullet,
  \begin{itemize}
  \item a dash,
    \begin{itemize}
    \item an asterisk,
      \begin{itemize}
      \item and a dot.
      \end{itemize}
    \end{itemize}
  \end{itemize}
\end{itemize}
\begin{description}
\item[Term] its description,
\item[Another term] and another, long enough to run on to a second line
  under the first.
\end{description}

\subsection{Notes}

A footnote\footnote{A note at the foot of the page.}, a mark set
apart\footnotemark{} with its text given after\footnotetext{The text of the
mark.}, and a note in the margin\marginpar{A margin note.} beside its line.

\subsection{Counters and lengths}

\newcounter{tick}
\setcounter{tick}{4}\addtocounter{tick}{3}\stepcounter{tick}
The counter is \arabic{tick}, \roman{tick}, \Roman{tick}, \alph{tick},
\Alph{tick} and \fnsymbol{footnote}; its value \the\value{tick}, and
\thetick{} as printed.
\newlength{\span}
\setlength{\span}{2cm}\addtolength{\span}{5mm}
\settowidth{\span}{a measured phrase}
A length set to a phrase's width: \the\span. The page's own:
\verb|\textwidth| is \the\textwidth, \verb|\parindent| \the\parindent, and
\verb|\baselineskip| \the\baselineskip.

\subsection{A document's own commands and blocks}

\newcommand{\greeting}[2][Dear]{#1 #2,}
\renewcommand{\greeting}[2][Dear]{#1~#2,}
\providecommand{\greeting}{never}
\newcommand*{\shout}[1]{\textbf{#1!}}
\newenvironment{note}[1][Note]{\par\noindent\textbf{#1.}\itshape}{\par}
\renewenvironment{note}[1][Note]{\par\noindent\textbf{#1:}\ \itshape}{\par}
\greeting{reader} \greeting[Hello]{world} \shout{loud}.
\begin{note}A block of the document's own.\end{note}
\begin{note}[Remark]With its optional argument.\end{note}
\def\pair#1#2{(#1,#2)}\let\couple\pair
\edef\built{\pair{a}{b}}
Definitions in TeX's own words: \pair{1}{2}, \couple{3}{4} and \built.
\expandafter\def\csname made by name\endcsname{made by name}
\csname made by name\endcsname, and
\ifx\pair\couple the two are the same\else they differ\fi;
\ifnum 3>2 three is more\fi; \ifdim 1cm>1mm a centimetre is longer\fi;
\ifcase 2 zero\or one\or two\else many\fi.

\subsection{Boxes}

\mbox{an mbox}, \makebox[3cm][l]{left in 3cm}, \makebox[3cm][c]{centred},
\fbox{an fbox}, \framebox[3cm][r]{right, framed}, \raisebox{1ex}{up} and
\raisebox{-1ex}{down}, a rule \rule{1cm}{2pt} and a strut\rule{0pt}{12pt}.
\parbox[t]{3cm}{A parbox, three centimetres wide, its text wrapped within
it.} \parbox[b]{3cm}{Another, standing on its last line.}
\newsavebox{\held}\savebox{\held}{kept}\usebox{\held} and \usebox{\held}.

\subsection{Tables}

\begin{table}[htbp]
  \centering
  \caption{LaTeX's own tabular, every rule it has.}\label{tab:kernel}
  \begin{tabular}{|l|c|r|p{3cm}|}
    \hline
    \multicolumn{4}{|c|}{A heading over every column} \\
    \hline
    left & centre & right & a paragraph column wraps its text \\
    \cline{2-3}
    a & b & 1.5 & short \\
    \hline\hline
    \multicolumn{2}{|l|}{two columns} & 3 & last \\
    \hline
  \end{tabular}
  \quad
  \begin{tabular}{@{}ll@{}}
    no & outer space \\
    at & either side
  \end{tabular}
\end{table}

\subsection{LaTeX's picture}

\begin{figure}[htbp]
  \centering
  \setlength{\unitlength}{1mm}
  \begin{picture}(60,30)
    \put(0,0){\line(1,0){60}}
    \put(0,0){\line(0,1){30}}
    \put(0,0){\line(2,1){40}}
    \put(10,25){\vector(1,0){20}}
    \put(45,15){\circle{10}}
    \put(45,15){\circle*{2}}
    \put(5,10){a label}
    \put(30,2){\framebox(20,8){framed}}
    \multiput(0,28)(5,0){7}{\line(0,1){2}}
    \qbezier(0,0)(30,30)(60,0)
  \end{picture}
  \caption{Lines, a vector, circles, a label, a framed box, a row of ticks and
    a curve, in LaTeX's own picture.}\label{fig:picture}
\end{figure}

\subsection{Mathematics}

In the line, $a^2 + b^2 = c^2$, \(x_i\), \begin{math}y\end{math}, and
\ensuremath{z} outside a formula; displayed:
\begin{displaymath}
  \sum_{k=0}^{n} \binom{n}{k} = 2^n, \qquad \prod_{i=1}^{n} i = n!,
  \qquad \lim_{x \to 0} \frac{\sin x}{x} = 1.
\end{displaymath}
LaTeX's own numbered and aligned equations:
\begin{eqnarray}
  f(x) & = & (x + 1)^2 \label{eq:square} \\
       & = & x^2 + 2x + 1 \nonumber
\end{eqnarray}
Every Greek letter: $\alpha \beta \gamma \delta \epsilon \varepsilon \zeta
\eta \theta \vartheta \iota \kappa \lambda \mu \nu \xi \pi \varpi \rho
\varrho \sigma \varsigma \tau \upsilon \phi \varphi \chi \psi \omega$ and
$\Gamma \Delta \Theta \Lambda \Xi \Pi \Sigma \Upsilon \Phi \Psi \Omega$.
Alphabets: $\mathrm{rm}\ \mathit{it}\ \mathbf{bf}\ \mathsf{sf}\ \mathtt{tt}\
\mathcal{CAL}\ \mathbb{BB}\ \mathfrak{Frak}$. Accents: $\hat{a}\ \check{a}\
\tilde{a}\ \acute{a}\ \grave{a}\ \dot{a}\ \ddot{a}\ \breve{a}\ \bar{a}\
\vec{a}\ \widehat{abc}\ \widetilde{abc}\ \overline{abc}\ \underline{abc}$.
Relations and operators: $\leq \geq \neq \approx \equiv \sim \simeq \cong
\propto \subset \supseteq \in \notin \ni \perp \parallel \mid \pm \mp
\times \div \cdot \circ \bullet \oplus \otimes \cup \cap \wedge \vee
\setminus$. Arrows: $\leftarrow \rightarrow \leftrightarrow \Leftarrow
\Rightarrow \Leftrightarrow \mapsto \uparrow \downarrow \longrightarrow
\hookrightarrow$. Dots: $1, \ldots, n$, $1 + \cdots + n$, and in a
matrix:
\[
  \left( \begin{array}{ccc}
    a_{11} & \cdots & a_{1n} \\
    \vdots & \ddots & \vdots \\
    a_{m1} & \cdots & a_{mn}
  \end{array} \right)
  \quad
  \overbrace{a + b + c}^{\text{three}}
  \quad
  \underbrace{x + y}_{\text{two}}
  \quad
  \sqrt[3]{x} \quad \sqrt{\frac{a}{b}}
\]
\[
  \stackrel{\text{def}}{=}
  \quad
  a \bmod b \quad a \equiv b \pmod{m}
  \quad
  \overbracket{p\,q}^{2} \quad \underparen{r\,s}_{2}
\]
\[
  \left\langle \frac{x}{y} \right\rangle
  \quad
  \Big( \big( x \big) \Big)
  \quad
  \int_0^\infty \oint \iint
  \quad
  \sum\limits_{i} \sum\nolimits_{j}
\]

\subsection{References}

Every kind of reference in one place: \cref{app:headings} is a heading,
equation~\eqref{eq:square} LaTeX's own, \cref{tab:kernel} a table,
\cref{fig:picture} a picture, item~\ref{item:last} an item, and
\cref{app:kernel} starts on page~\pageref{app:kernel}.

